@startuml ABTS_Generation_Flow
!theme blueprint
title Cramer CMS - ABTS AI Content Generation Flow

skinparam {
    BackgroundColor #1a1a2e
    TitleFontColor #ffffff
    TitleFontSize 20
    DefaultFontColor #e8e8e8
    ArrowColor #64b5f6
    ActorBackgroundColor #4caf50
    RectangleBackgroundColor #37474f
    RectangleBorderColor #78909c
    NoteBackgroundColor #424242
    NoteFontColor #ffffff
}

actor "Admin User" as Admin #coral

rectangle "Frontend - AI Studio" {
    rectangle "Step 1: Config" as Step1 {
        (Skill Selection)
        (Model Selection)
        (Temperature)
        (Reasoning Toggle)
    }
    
    rectangle "Step 2: Parts" as Step2 {
        (Part Selection)
        (Question Types per Part)
        (Topic per Part)
        (Randomize Option)
    }
    
    rectangle "Step 3: Generate" as Step3 {
        (SSE Streaming Display)
        (Progress Bar)
        (Reasoning Tokens View)
        (Cancel Button)
    }
    
    rectangle "Step 4: Preview" as Step4 {
        (Content Preview)
        (Validation Issues List)
        (Issue Selection)
    }
    
    rectangle "Step 5: Refine" as Step5 {
        (Agent 2 Refinement)
        (Patch Stream)
        (Re-validation)
    }
    
    rectangle "Step 6: Save" as Step6 {
        (Set Selection)
        (Test Selection)
        (Save to Database)
    }
    
    [useABTSStore] as ABTSStore
}

rectangle "Backend - ABTS Services" {
    [ABTSController] as ABTSCtrl
    [ABTSService] as ABTSSvc
    [PromptBuilderService] as PromptSvc
    [OpenRouterClient] as ORClient
    [JsonValidatorService] as ValidatorSvc
    [RefinementService] as RefineSvc
    [JsonPatcher] as Patcher
}

cloud "AI Provider" {
    [OpenRouter API\n(400+ models)] as OpenRouter
}

database "Database" {
    [sections]
    [questions]
}

' Wizard Flow
Admin --> Step1 : Open AI Studio
Step1 --> Step2 : Next
Step2 --> Step3 : Generate
Step3 --> Step4 : View Results
Step4 --> Step5 : Fix Issues
Step5 --> Step4 : Re-validate
Step4 --> Step6 : Save
Step6 --> sections : Persist

' Generation Flow (Two-Pass)
Step3 --> ABTSCtrl : POST /generate/{skill}/stream
ABTSCtrl --> ABTSSvc : generateWithStream(request, emitter, cancelled)
ABTSSvc --> PromptSvc : Build Phase 1 prompt (passage/transcript)
PromptSvc --> ABTSSvc : Return prompt
ABTSSvc --> ORClient : streamingCall(prompt, schema)
ORClient --> OpenRouter : SSE Request
OpenRouter --> ORClient : Stream tokens
ORClient --> ABTSSvc : onContentChunk, onReasoningChunk
ABTSSvc --> Step3 : SSE events (AI_CHUNK, AI_THINKING)

ABTSSvc --> PromptSvc : Build Phase 2 prompt (questions)
PromptSvc --> ABTSSvc : Return prompt with Phase 1 content
ABTSSvc --> ORClient : streamingCall(prompt, schema)
ORClient --> OpenRouter : SSE Request

' Validation
ABTSSvc --> ValidatorSvc : validate(content)
ValidatorSvc --> ABTSStore : Return issues list

' Refinement Flow
Step5 --> ABTSCtrl : POST /refine/stream
ABTSCtrl --> RefineSvc : refineContent(content, issues)
RefineSvc --> ORClient : Generate patches via Agent 2
ORClient --> OpenRouter : AI Request
OpenRouter --> RefineSvc : Patch instructions
RefineSvc --> Patcher : Apply patches (REPLACE/INSERT/APPEND)
Patcher --> RefineSvc : Updated content
RefineSvc --> ValidatorSvc : Re-validate
ValidatorSvc --> ABTSStore : Updated issues

' Save Flow
Step6 --> ABTSCtrl : POST /save
ABTSCtrl --> ABTSSvc : saveContent(request)
ABTSSvc --> sections : INSERT section
ABTSSvc --> questions : INSERT questions

note right of ABTSSvc
  **Two-Pass Strategy:**
  
  **Phase 1:** Generate passage/transcript
  - Topic-focused content
  - Paragraph labeling (A, B, C...)
  - Speaker labels (Listening)
  
  **Phase 2:** Generate questions
  - Based on Phase 1 content
  - Question numbering (1-40)
  - Answer extraction
end note

note bottom of ValidatorSvc
  **Validation Layers:**
  1. Schema (JSON structure)
  2. Content (word limits, counts)
  3. Business Rules (Q numbering)
  
  **Issue Categories:**
  - question_numbering
  - answer_format
  - missing_field
  - content_length
end note

note left of Patcher
  **Patch Operations:**
  - REPLACE: Replace value at path
  - INSERT: Insert into array
  - APPEND: Append to string/array
end note

@enduml
